---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    question: "What counts as a 'valid public watch hour' for YouTube monetization?",
    answer: "Valid public watch hours are hours generated from public long-form videos and public live streams (VODs) watched by real users during the preceding 365 days. Watch time from unlisted videos, private videos, deleted videos, Google Ads video campaigns, and views from the YouTube Shorts feed do NOT count toward the 4,000-hour threshold."
  },
  {
    question: "Do YouTube Shorts views count toward the 4,000 watch hours requirement?",
    answer: "No. Watch hours accrued from viewers watching vertical videos in the YouTube Shorts feed do not count toward the 4,000 valid public watch hours requirement. However, creators focusing primarily on Shorts can alternatively qualify for full YouTube Partner Program monetization by achieving 10 million valid public Shorts views within the last 90 days alongside 1,000 subscribers."
  },
  {
    question: "What is the difference between the 3,000-hour and 4,000-hour YPP milestones?",
    answer: "The 3,000-hour milestone (along with 500 subscribers and 3 valid public uploads in the last 90 days) unlocks the early-access YouTube Partner Program tier in eligible countries. This tier provides Fan Funding features—including Channel Memberships, Super Chat, Super Stickers, Super Thanks, and YouTube Shopping. The 4,000-hour milestone (along with 1,000 subscribers) unlocks full YouTube ad revenue sharing from Watch Page ads and YouTube Premium."
  },
  {
    question: "Why is my watch time in YouTube Studio Analytics higher than on the Earn tab?",
    answer: "The general Analytics tab displays lifetime watch time across all video types, including private, unlisted, deleted, and Shorts feed views. The Earn tab strictly filters for 'valid public watch hours' accumulated exclusively on public long-form content within a rolling 365-day window. The Earn tab also updates on a 24- to 72-hour delay to verify view validity."
  },
  {
    question: "How does the 365-day rolling window affect my watch hours?",
    answer: "YouTube evaluates monetization watch hours over a rolling 365-day window, not a calendar year. Each day, the watch hours you accumulated exactly 366 days ago expire from your monetization tally. To make forward progress, your channel must generate more new watch hours each day than the watch hours that expire from 366 days prior."
  },
  {
    question: "Does reaching 4,000 watch hours guarantee approval into the YouTube Partner Program?",
    answer: "No. Reaching 4,000 valid public watch hours and 1,000 subscribers only makes your channel eligible to apply. Your channel must then pass a human review process ensuring compliance with YouTube Channel Monetization Policies, Community Guidelines, Copyright rules, and Google AdSense Terms of Service."
  }
];

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', item: '/' },
  { name: 'Tools', item: '/tools' },
  { name: 'YouTube Watch Time Calculator', item: '/tools/youtube-watch-time-calculator' }
];

const origin = Astro.site ? Astro.site.origin : "https://creatorsfeel.com";
const canonicalUrl = new URL(Astro.url.pathname, origin).href;

const softwareSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "SoftwareApplication",
      "@id": `${canonicalUrl}#application`,
      "name": "YouTube Watch Time Calculator",
      "url": canonicalUrl,
      "operatingSystem": "All",
      "applicationCategory": "BusinessApplication",
      "description": "Free YouTube Watch Time Calculator. Track progress toward 3,000 and 4,000 valid public watch hours, calculate remaining hours, and project your YPP monetization completion date.",
      "offers": {
        "@type": "Offer",
        "price": "0.00",
        "priceCurrency": "USD"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "@id": `${canonicalUrl}#faq`,
      "mainEntity": faqs.map(faq => ({
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": faq.question,
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": faq.answer
        }
      }))
    }
  ]
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="YouTube Watch Time Calculator - Track 4,000 Hours Milestone"
  description="Free YouTube Watch Time Calculator. Track progress toward 3,000 and 4,000 valid public watch hours, calculate remaining hours, and project your YPP monetization completion date."
  canonicalUrl={canonicalUrl}
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" slot="meta" set:html={JSON.stringify(softwareSchema)} />

  <div class="tool-page-wrapper">
    
    <!-- 1. HERO SECTION (Centered Max-Width 820px) -->
    <header class="tool-hero-section">
      <div class="container hero-inner">
        
        <!-- Breadcrumbs at top -->
        <div class="hero-breadcrumbs">
          <Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs} />
        </div>

        <!-- Pill Badge with SVG Icon (Zero Emojis) -->
        <div class="hero-badge">
          <span class="badge-icon-tool">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="tool-svg" aria-hidden="true">
              <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" />
              <polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14" />
            </svg>
          </span>
          <span class="badge-title">YouTube Monetization & Watch Time Tracker</span>
          <span class="badge-pill-free">Free Tool</span>
        </div>

        <!-- Main Headline -->
        <h1 class="hero-headline">
          YouTube Watch Time <span class="gradient-text">Calculator</span>
        </h1>

        <!-- Short Description -->
        <p class="hero-desc">
          Track your progress toward 3,000 and 4,000 valid public watch hours. Calculate remaining hours, estimated days left, and your projected milestone completion date.
        </p>

        <!-- Feature Chips Row (Zero Emojis - Clean SVG Icons) -->
        <div class="hero-features-row">
          <span class="feature-chip">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="chip-svg" aria-hidden="true">
              <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" />
              <polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14" />
            </svg>
            3,000 & 4,000 Hour Goals
          </span>
          <span class="feature-chip">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="chip-svg" aria-hidden="true">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M6.75 3v2.25M17.25 3v2.253 3.75h18M4.5 7.5h15a2.25 2.25 0 0 1 2.25 2.25v10.5A2.25 2.25 0 0 1 19.5 22.5h-15A2.25 2.25 0 0 1 2.25 20.25V9.75A2.25 2.25 0 0 1 4.5 7.5Z" />
            </svg>
            Completion Date Forecast
          </span>
          <span class="feature-chip">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="chip-svg" aria-hidden="true">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M3.75 13.5l10.5-11.25L12 10.5h8.25L9.75 21.75 12 13.5H3.75z" />
            </svg>
            Live Progress Gauge
          </span>
          <span class="feature-chip">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="chip-svg" aria-hidden="true">
              <rect x="3" y="11" width="18" height="11" rx="2" ry="2" />
              <path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4" />
            </svg>
            100% In-Browser Privacy
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- 2. MAIN TOOL SECTION (Container Max-Width 940px) -->
    <section class="tool-main-section" aria-label="YouTube Watch Time Calculator Interface">
      <div class="container tool-card-container">
        
        <!-- The Prominent SaaS Tool Card -->
        <div class="saas-tool-card">
          
          <!-- Card Header Bar -->
          <div class="card-header-bar">
            <div class="card-title-meta">
              <span class="tool-section-title">Watch Time Parameters</span>
              <span class="tool-section-sub">Enter your eligible public watch hours and daily pace from YouTube Studio</span>
            </div>

            <!-- Live Status & Reset Bar -->
            <div class="header-action-wrap">
              <div class="live-status-badge">
                <span class="live-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <span class="live-text">Live Projection</span>
              </div>
              <button type="button" class="btn-reset-tool" id="btn-reset" title="Reset inputs to sample values">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="reset-svg" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M16.023 9.348h4.992v-.001M2.985 19.644v-4.992m0 0h4.992m-4.993 0 3.181 3.183a8.25 8.25 0 0 0 13.803-3.7M4.031 9.865a8.25 8.25 0 0 1 13.803-3.7l3.181 3.182m0-4.991v4.99" />
                </svg>
                <span>Reset</span>
              </button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Essential Inputs Grid (Only 3 Inputs) -->
          <div class="calculator-inputs-grid">
            
            <!-- Field 1: Current Valid Public Watch Hours -->
            <div class="input-field-group">
              <div class="field-label-row">
                <label for="input-current-hours" class="field-label">
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="label-svg" aria-hidden="true">
                    <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/>
                    <polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"/>
                  </svg>
                  <span>Current Valid Public Watch Hours</span>
                  <span class="badge-tag-required">Required</span>
                </label>
              </div>
              <div class="input-wrapper">
                <input
                  type="number"
                  id="input-current-hours"
                  class="styled-input"
                  placeholder="Enter current valid watch hours"
                  min="0"
                  step="1"
                  value="1250"
                  aria-describedby="desc-current-hours"
                />
              </div>
              <p class="field-helper-text" id="desc-current-hours">
                Eligible public watch hours recorded in your YouTube Studio Earn tab (rolling 365 days).
              </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Field 2: Average Daily Watch Hours -->
            <div class="input-field-group">
              <div class="field-label-row">
                <label for="input-daily-hours" class="field-label">
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="label-svg" aria-hidden="true">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 6v6h4.5m4.5 0a9 9 0 1 1-18 0 9 9 0 0 1 18 0Z" />
                  </svg>
                  <span>Average Daily Watch Hours</span>
                  <span class="badge-tag-required">Required</span>
                </label>
              </div>
              <div class="input-wrapper">
                <input
                  type="number"
                  id="input-daily-hours"
                  class="styled-input"
                  placeholder="Enter average daily watch hours"
                  min="0"
                  step="0.1"
                  value="12.5"
                  aria-describedby="desc-daily-hours"
                />
              </div>
              <p class="field-helper-text" id="desc-daily-hours">
                Average daily eligible watch hours (e.g., total watch hours in past 28 days ÷ 28).
              </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Field 3: Target Watch Hours Milestone Selector -->
            <div class="input-field-group full-width-field">
              <div class="field-label-row">
                <span class="field-label">
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="label-svg" aria-hidden="true">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M3 13.125C3 12.504 3.504 12 4.125 12h2.25c.621 0 1.125.504 1.125 1.125v6.75C7.5 20.496 6.996 21 6.375 21h-2.25A1.125 1.125 0 0 1 3 19.875v-6.75ZM9.75 8.625c0-.621.504-1.125 1.125-1.125h2.25c.621 0 1.125.504 1.125 1.125v11.25c0 .621-.504 1.125-1.125 1.125h-2.25a1.125 1.125 0 0 1-1.125-1.125V8.625ZM16.5 4.125c0-.621.504-1.125 1.125-1.125h2.25C20.496 3 21 3.504 21 4.125v15.75c0 .621-.504 1.125-1.125 1.125h-2.25a1.125 1.125 0 0 1-1.125-1.125V4.125Z" />
                  </svg>
                  <span>Target Watch Hours Milestone</span>
                </span>
                <span class="field-helper-badge">YouTube Partner Program</span>
              </div>
              
              <div class="target-tabs-row" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Select target watch hours milestone">
                <button
                  type="button"
                  class="target-tab active"
                  data-target="4000"
                  aria-pressed="true"
                >
                  <div class="target-tab-title">
                    <span class="target-tab-val">4,000 Hours</span>
                    <span class="target-tier-badge tier-full">Full YPP Tier</span>
                  </div>
                  <span class="target-tab-desc">Unlocks Watch Page & Shorts Ad Revenue (Requires 1,000 subs)</span>
                </button>

                <button
                  type="button"
                  class="target-tab"
                  data-target="3000"
                  aria-pressed="false"
                >
                  <div class="target-tab-title">
                    <span class="target-tab-val">3,000 Hours</span>
                    <span class="target-tier-badge tier-fan">Fan Funding Tier</span>
                  </div>
                  <span class="target-tab-desc">Unlocks Memberships, Supers & Shopping (Requires 500 subs)</span>
                </button>
              </div>

              <p class="field-helper-text">
                Eligibility requirements and available features vary by YouTube Partner Program tier and country.
              </p>
            </div>

          </div>

          <!-- Divider -->
          <div class="card-divider"></div>

          <!-- Results Dashboard -->
          <div class="results-dashboard-wrapper">
            
            <div class="results-header-row">
              <span class="results-heading-badge" id="badge-target-header">Progress to 4,000 Watch Hours</span>
              <span class="results-calc-pill">365-Day Rolling Model</span>
            </div>

            <!-- Milestone Progress Bar Card -->
            <div class="progress-gauge-card">
              <div class="progress-gauge-top">
                <div class="gauge-stats">
                  <span class="gauge-current-text" id="gauge-ratio-text">1,250 / 4,000 Hours</span>
                  <span class="gauge-pct-badge" id="gauge-pct-badge">31.3%</span>
                </div>
                <span class="gauge-sub-label">Milestone Progress</span>
              </div>

              <div class="progress-track-bar">
                <div class="progress-fill-glow" id="progress-bar-fill" style="width: 31.3%;"></div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Target Achieved Celebration Banner (Hidden by default, shown if current >= target) -->
            <div class="achieved-alert-banner" id="achieved-banner" style="display: none;" role="status">
              <div class="achieved-icon-circle">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" class="achieved-svg" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m4.5 12.75 6 6 9-13.5" />
                </svg>
              </div>
              <div class="achieved-text-wrap">
                <strong class="achieved-heading">Milestone Reached! Target Watch Hours Met</strong>
                <p class="achieved-desc">
                  Your channel has reached or exceeded this watch-hour threshold. Verify that you also fulfill subscriber requirements and adhere to all YouTube Channel Monetization Policies before applying.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- 4 Essential Result Metric Cards Grid -->
            <div class="results-cards-grid">
              
              <!-- Card 1: Remaining Hours to Reach Target (Hero) -->
              <div class="result-metric-card card-hero-remaining">
                <div class="metric-card-top">
                  <span class="metric-label">Remaining Hours</span>
                  <span class="metric-tag tag-brand">Goal Gap</span>
                </div>
                <div class="metric-value-display text-hero" id="val-remaining-hours">2,750</div>
                <div class="metric-sub-text" id="sub-remaining-detail">Hours left to reach 4,000 threshold</div>
              </div>

              <!-- Card 2: Estimated Days Remaining -->
              <div class="result-metric-card card-days-left">
                <div class="metric-card-top">
                  <span class="metric-label">Days to Target</span>
                  <span class="metric-tag tag-blue">Pacing Forecast</span>
                </div>
                <div class="metric-value-display text-blue" id="val-days-remaining">220 Days</div>
                <div class="metric-sub-text" id="sub-days-detail">Based on 12.5 daily watch hours</div>
              </div>

              <!-- Card 3: Estimated Completion Date -->
              <div class="result-metric-card card-date-projected">
                <div class="metric-card-top">
                  <span class="metric-label">Projected Date</span>
                  <span class="metric-tag tag-green">Estimated Finish</span>
                </div>
                <div class="metric-value-display text-green" id="val-projected-date">May 30, 2027</div>
                <div class="metric-sub-text" id="sub-date-detail">Calculated from today at current pace</div>
              </div>

              <!-- Card 4: Current Valid Hours -->
              <div class="result-metric-card card-current-hours">
                <div class="metric-card-top">
                  <span class="metric-label">Current Valid Hours</span>
                  <span class="metric-tag tag-purple">Studio Baseline</span>
                </div>
                <div class="metric-value-display text-purple" id="val-current-display">1,250</div>
                <div class="metric-sub-text" id="sub-current-detail">31.3% of 4,000 hour target</div>
              </div>

            </div>

            <!-- Transparent Calculation & Policy Disclaimer Card -->
            <div class="results-explanation-card">
              <div class="explanation-title-row">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="exp-svg" aria-hidden="true">
                  <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/>
                  <line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12" y2="12"/>
                  <line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12.01" y2="8"/>
                </svg>
                <strong class="exp-heading">Calculation Model & Monetization Notice</strong>
              </div>

              <p class="exp-summary" id="res-explanation-text">
                Calculation: <span class="formula-text">4,000 target − 1,250 current = 2,750 remaining hours</span>. At <span class="formula-text">12.5 hours/day</span>, reaching the milestone will take an estimated <span class="formula-text">220 days</span>.
              </p>

              <p class="exp-disclaimer">
                <strong>Notice:</strong> This projection assumes a constant daily accumulation pace. YouTube watch hours expire on a 365-day rolling basis (hours earned over 365 days ago fall off daily). Reaching watch-hour and subscriber milestones makes your channel eligible to apply, but does not guarantee monetization approval. All channels undergo human review to verify compliance with YouTube's Channel Monetization Policies.
              </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Actions Row: Copy Summary Button -->
            <div class="results-action-row">
              <button type="button" id="btn-copy-summary" class="btn-copy-summary" title="Copy watch time forecast to clipboard">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="copy-svg" aria-hidden="true">
                  <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"/>
                  <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"/>
                </svg>
                <span id="copy-summary-label">Copy Milestone Forecast</span>
              </button>
            </div>

          </div>

        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 3. COMPREHENSIVE EDITORIAL & SEO CONTENT (Max-Width 940px) -->
    <section class="tool-content-section" aria-label="YouTube Watch Time Guide and Monetization Best Practices">
      <div class="container content-inner-container">
        
        <!-- Editorial Articles & Guidelines Card -->
        <div class="content-card">
          
          <div class="editorial-block">
            <span class="content-pill">YouTube Monetization Guide</span>
            
            <h2>What Is a YouTube Watch Time Calculator and How Does It Work?</h2>
            <p>
              A <strong>YouTube Watch Time Calculator</strong> is a strategic planning utility designed to help emerging creators monitor their progress toward the YouTube Partner Program (YPP) watch-hour milestones. Reaching YouTube's watch-time thresholds is widely considered the most demanding requirement for monetization. A dedicated <strong>YouTube watch hours calculator</strong> translates your current valid public watch hours and daily accumulation rates into actionable milestones, estimating the exact days remaining until eligibility.
            </p>
            <p>
              Rather than checking YouTube Studio with uncertainty or worrying whether your channel will beat the rolling 365-day expiration cliff, our <strong>calculate YouTube watch time</strong> tool provides mathematically transparent projections. By evaluating your daily accumulation velocity against the 3,000-hour or 4,000-hour targets, you can adjust your upload schedule, refine viewer retention strategies, and plan your monetization application with confidence.
            </p>

            <h2>How to Calculate Remaining Watch Hours and Estimated Time to Monetization</h2>
            <p>
              Estimating your timeline to YouTube monetization relies on three straightforward mathematical equations:
            </p>
            <ul class="styled-list">
              <li><strong>1. Remaining Watch Hours:</strong> <span class="formula-text">Remaining Hours = max(0, Target Hours − Current Valid Watch Hours)</span>. If your target is 4,000 hours and your channel has accumulated 1,500 valid hours, your remaining requirement is 2,500 hours. If your current hours exceed the target, the result is cleanly capped at zero.</li>
              <li><strong>2. Estimated Days Remaining:</strong> <span class="formula-text">Estimated Days = ceil(Remaining Hours ÷ Average Daily Watch Hours)</span>. If you need 2,500 hours and generate an average of 12.5 watch hours per day, the remaining duration is 2,500 ÷ 12.5 = 200 days. If daily watch hours equal zero, a completion date cannot be estimated until watch time begins accumulating.</li>
              <li><strong>3. Percentage Progress:</strong> <span class="formula-text">Progress % = min(100, [Current Valid Watch Hours ÷ Target Hours] × 100)</span>. For 1,500 hours toward a 4,000-hour target, progress is exactly 37.5%.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
              Our calculator also adds the estimated days directly to today's date, providing a concrete projected calendar completion date so you can set realistic creator goals.
            </p>

            <h2>Valid Public Watch Hours vs. Total Analytics Watch Time: Critical Differences</h2>
            <p>
              A frequent source of heartbreak for growing creators is discovering a discrepancy between the watch time displayed on their YouTube Studio "Analytics" tab and the hours recorded on their "Earn" tab. Understanding the strict boundaries of <strong>valid public watch hours</strong> is critical for accurate tracking:
            </p>
            <ul class="styled-list">
              <li><strong>Total Watch Time (Analytics Tab):</strong> Measures all cumulative minutes and hours watched across every video on your channel, regardless of visibility, video format, or traffic source. This includes private videos, unlisted videos, deleted videos, YouTube Shorts feed views, and views generated through paid Google Ads campaigns.</li>
              <li><strong>Valid Public Watch Hours (Earn Tab):</strong> The exclusively audited metric used by YouTube for Partner Program eligibility. Under official guidelines, watch hours qualify only if they originate from public long-form videos or public live stream recordings (VODs) watched by real users during the preceding 365 days.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Which Watch Time Does NOT Count Toward YouTube Monetization?</h2>
            <p>
              Under official <a href="https://support.google.com/youtube/answer/72851" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">YouTube Partner Program eligibility guidelines</a>, several common view categories are explicitly disqualified from the 4,000-hour requirement:
            </p>
            <ul class="styled-list">
              <li><strong>YouTube Shorts Feed Views:</strong> Watch time accumulated from vertical videos swiped through in the dedicated YouTube Shorts player does not count toward the 4,000-hour threshold. Shorts views only count toward the alternative 10-million Shorts view milestone.</li>
              <li><strong>Private and Unlisted Videos:</strong> If you switch a public video to private or unlisted, its watch hours are immediately deducted from your Earn tab tally.</li>
              <li><strong>Deleted Videos:</strong> Deleting a video permanently wipes all accumulated watch hours associated with that video from your monetization meter. If you need to trim an awkward section from an existing video, use YouTube's native editor rather than deleting and re-uploading.</li>
              <li><strong>Google Ads Video Campaigns:</strong> Running paid promotional ads through Google Ads (formerly YouTube TrueView) generates views, but those paid view hours do not qualify as valid organic watch time.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>The 3,000-Hour vs. 4,000-Hour Milestones Explained</h2>
            <p>
              YouTube operates a two-tiered Partner Program framework with distinct eligibility milestones and unlocked monetization features:
            </p>
            <ul class="styled-list">
              <li><strong>The 3,000-Hour Milestone (Fan Funding Tier):</strong> Introduced to help creators monetize earlier in their journey. Requirements: 3,000 valid public watch hours in the past 365 days (or 3 million public Shorts views in 90 days), 500 subscribers, and 3 valid public uploads in the last 90 days. Unlocks: Channel Memberships, Super Chat, Super Stickers, Super Thanks, and YouTube Shopping affiliate features. It does <em>not</em> unlock ad revenue sharing.</li>
              <li><strong>The 4,000-Hour Milestone (Full YPP Tier):</strong> The gold-standard monetization milestone. Requirements: 4,000 valid public watch hours in the past 365 days (or 10 million public Shorts views in 90 days) and 1,000 subscribers. Unlocks: Full revenue sharing from Watch Page advertisements, YouTube Shorts feed advertisements, and YouTube Premium subscription revenue splits.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
              Once you unlock the full tier, you can project your monthly AdSense revenue using our <a href="/tools/youtube-earnings-calculator">YouTube Earnings Calculator</a> and evaluate advertiser rates with our <a href="/tools/youtube-cpm-calculator">YouTube CPM Calculator</a>.
            </p>

            <h2>The Rolling 365-Day Window: Why Old Watch Hours Expire</h2>
            <p>
              Many creators mistakenly believe they have until December 31st or a fixed calendar year to accumulate 4,000 hours. In reality, YouTube measures watch time on a <strong>rolling 365-day basis</strong>:
            </p>
            <p>
              Every single day, the watch hours your channel earned exactly 366 days ago expire and fall off your Earn tab. If your channel experienced a viral surge 11 months ago that generated 1,500 hours, those hours will vanish one year after they occurred unless your daily watch hours match or exceed that historical pace. Understanding this rolling mechanism is essential to prevent watch-hour stagnation.
            </p>

            <h2>Practical Ways Creators Can Accelerate Watch Time Growth</h2>
            <p>
              To outpace the 365-day expiration rate and hit 4,000 watch hours faster, apply these proven creator strategies:
            </p>
            <ul class="styled-list">
